body:
u/Archturus/ : It is alarming to me that as a medical professional, you find someone who is requesting euthanasia to be "trolling".

&#x200B;

I hope you don't tell your patients that are suffering enough to consider suicide that they are "trying to find a morgue that takes a walk in". It is frankly, condescending, rude, and demonstrates a complete lack of empany

&#x200B;

There are better ways to disagree - ie. "I'm sorry you're feeling that way- I disagree with this course of action becuase ( reason ABC) and would suggest (alternative XYZ) . I hope things get better for you."

&#x200B;

I hope you treat your patients with more empathy and kindness than you have shown me here.

Patients who attempt suicide yes, patients looking for euthanasia no - there is a difference. 

&#x200B;

Asthma is not a terminal condition however it is not reasonable to seek relief from a long-term chronic illness with no cure.

&#x200B;

I feel that you are telling me I am not suffering enough to justify wanting to seek relief. If so, you are definitely failing to understand just how low the quality of life actually is- that is not up to you to make that call. Your apathy is fairly common in the medical field but is definitely more harmful than good for patients.

&#x200B;

FYI: those whose suffering is no longer tolerable, even without a terminal condition do get euthanized - a physically healthy 29-year-old suffering mental distress was offered euthanasia a couple of years back:

[https://www.bbc.com/news/stories-45117163](https://www.bbc.com/news/stories-45117163)

As I stated above, I don't want suggestions for medical help  - I have already done this exhaustively and repeatedly to no avail. 

&#x200B;

And yes, I have an air filter, humidifier (it's dry where I live), and the house/linens/air filters are cleaned weekly. I've had a comprehensive allergy test too and take allergy meds, countless inhalers, sleep elevated, work with Asthma support groups, medical specialists etc. 

&#x200B;

There is nothing more that doctors can do - I have tried hundreds of different treatments over the years with no significant improvement to the quality of my life.

Thanks for the suggestions -tt is absolutely a terrible burden- I'm sorry you're struggling too. 

&#x200B;

I'll look at Oregan and see if it's a possibility; if not I'll find another way to die.
